<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Daehan Flour buys 21,500T of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Daehan Flour buys 21,500T of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Daehan Flour Mills Co Ltd said it bought 21,500 tonnes of U.S. No.1 wheat on Tuesday from Japanese trading house Mitsubishi Corp.  </p>
<p>A company official said the 21,500 tonnes of U.S. wheat was split into four lots -- 5,000 tonnes of western white/soft white (ordinary), 1,000 tonnes of western white/soft white wheat (protein minimum 10.0 percent), 7,000 tonnes of hard red winter wheat (protein minimum 11.5 percent), and 8,500 tonnes of dark northern spring wheat (protein minimum 14 percent).</p>
<p>Shipment was set for September 5-October 5 to the western port of Inchon.</p>
<p>Details for the results are as follow:</p>
<p>  Type of Wheat		   Tonne	Price/T (FOB)</p>
<p>  Western White/Soft White    5,000	 $133.90</p>
<p>  Western White		   1,000	 $134.65</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter		 7,000	 $136.80</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring	  8,500	 $166.80</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
